.TH B 1
.SH NAME
B \- open a file in the running text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B B
.I file...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I B
asks whatever editor is currently listening on
.B /cmd/clone
to open each
.IR file .
Relative paths are resolved against the current working directory
first.
.PP
This is the same convention Plan 9's own
.B B
uses for Acme: a small command-line hook so other tools and scripts
can hand a file to the editor already on screen, rather than starting
a new one.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/B.b
